***REMOVED******REMOVED*** 🏪 State Management Strategy

**STRICT** separation of concerns across different state management solutions:

***REMOVED******REMOVED******REMOVED*** 1. React Query - Server State

**USE FOR**: Data fetching, caching, synchronization with server

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Server state management
const useMovie = (id: string) => {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ["movie", id],
    queryFn: () => movieAPI.getById(id),
    staleTime: 10 * 60 * 1000, // 10 minutes
    enabled: !!id,
  });
};

const useMovies = (filters: MovieFilters) => {
  return useInfiniteQuery({
    queryKey: ["movies", filters],
    queryFn: ({ pageParam = 1 }) => movieAPI.getMovies(filters, pageParam),
    getNextPageParam: (lastPage) => lastPage.nextPage,
  });
};
```

***REMOVED******REMOVED******REMOVED*** 2. Zustand - Client State

**USE FOR**: UI preferences, filters, local application state

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Client state management
interface MovieFilterStore {
  filters: MovieFilters;
  setFilter: (key: keyof MovieFilters, value: any) => void;
  resetFilters: () => void;
  applyPreset: (preset: FilterPreset) => void;
}

const useMovieFilterStore = create<MovieFilterStore>((set) => ({
  filters: defaultFilters,
  setFilter: (key, value) =>
    set((state) => ({
      filters: { ...state.filters, [key]: value },
    })),
  resetFilters: () => set({ filters: defaultFilters }),
  applyPreset: (preset) => set({ filters: preset.filters }),
}));
```

